.TH DDNSD 8 "October 2026" "ddnsd 0.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ddnsd \- dynamic DNS daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddnsd
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.br
.B ddnsd dry\-run
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ddnsd
periodically finds this host's public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and keeps the
A and AAAA records of one or more domains pointed at them, using the
Cloudflare and No-IP DNS providers.
.PP
Addresses are found with HTTP echo services (icanhazip, ipify or custom URLs)
or from the global addresses of local network interfaces, tried in the
configured order for each address family.
.PP
When a provider rejects an update in a way that needs the configuration to be
fixed, such as invalid credentials, the daemon stops updating that provider,
and exits once all providers have been rejected. After server errors it waits
as long as the provider asks before updating that provider again.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dry\-run
Resolve the public addresses once and, for each provider, print the current
records and the changes an update would make, without making them. Only reads
from the providers. Exits with a non-zero status if any provider failed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIconfig\fR
Read the configuration from
.IR config .
The default is
.IR /etc/ddnsd.toml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ddnsd.toml
The TOML configuration file. It contains provider credentials and must not be
readable by group or others, e.g. mode 0600.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.toml
An example configuration describing all settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.B debug
or
.BR ddnsd=debug ;
the default is
.BR info .
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and start the service:
.PP
.nf
.RS
install \-m 600 /usr/share/doc/ddnsd/examples/ddnsd.example.toml /etc/ddnsd.toml
editor /etc/ddnsd.toml
systemctl start ddnsd
.RE
.fi
